//? Title: Patience sort: actual piles and heap sources
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Each incoming value goes to the leftmost pile whose top is greater than or equal
to it. Binary search locates that pile. A min-heap then merges pile tops,
breaking equal-value heap ties by pile index. Pile count equals the strictly
increasing LIS length, including when values repeat; it does not equal the
nondecreasing subsequence length. Sorting is O(n log n); retaining every top
snapshot can require quadratic history. No external dataset is appropriate for
the mechanism.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

Each incoming value goes to the leftmost pile whose top is greater than or equal
to it. Binary search locates that pile. A min-heap then merges pile tops,
breaking equal-value heap ties by pile index. Pile count equals the strictly
increasing LIS length, including when values repeat; it does not equal the
nondecreasing subsequence length. Sorting is O(n log n); retaining every top
snapshot can require quadratic history. No external dataset is appropriate for
the mechanism.

$$ L_i=1+\max_{j<i,\ a_j<a_i} L_j,\qquad \operatorname{LIS}(a)=\max_i L_i. $$

The maximum over an empty predecessor set is zero; empty input has LIS length
zero. This independent quadratic recurrence is used in tests, not to populate
the captured pile history.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/patience_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <iostream>
#include <sstream>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <numeric>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/patience_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::patience_sort_trace({3, 1, 2, 2});
    std::print("| incoming | actual pile | top comparisons | actual tops |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.deals)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", r.value, r.pile, r.comparisons,
                   r.tops);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual completed piles\n{}", t.piles));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual heap source ids\n{}", t.extracted_piles));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0}, std::format("Actual sorted values\n{}", t.sorted));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/patience_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
